A||N||8||Daleford||Want to shoot my Fiero/Kitcar. digital camera questions||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-24-2001||07:33 PM||||I know a bit about photography and 35 mm cameras.  What I don't know about are digital cameras. I would like to be able to post pics like the big guys.  Would I be able to do this with any digital camera?   <BR>Here in Canada I have noticed prices usually are around the 3-4 hundred range. I see a boxing day sale at a local discount chain has them on for --$75.--!! Would it be possible that this camera would suit my needs?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||AusFiero||12-24-2001||07:37 PM||||Depends what you want to use it for. My Kodak dc4800 does everything an SLR will do and has a resolution of 3.1 megapixels. I can also change iso settings etc.<BR>Look for a cam with at least 1.3 megapixels if wanting clear photographs.<BR>Hope that helps.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000002||GTFiero1||12-24-2001||07:41 PM||||75 dollars is probably gonna be a cheap quality camera. i'd recommend gttin closer to a 200 dollars||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou||12-24-2001||08:07 PM||||Get a 1 megapixel or better camera make sure that you get the cables that connect to the computer with it. Check ebay the older models  are an excellent buy these days.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||12-24-2001||08:53 PM||||I love mine that uses regular floppy disks for media. I can load or send pics straight from my floppy drive, no downloading or anything.Dont even need the camera hooked up. That type will run $400 and up. I think most of the type that use memory cards have to be transfered to a file or something first from the camera before you can store or send them out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||12-24-2001||09:08 PM||||A test and an example of a cheapo digital camera that I just bought for e-mailing family photos.  Bought one for each of my kids and for each of my parents so that we can e-mail photos to each other.  $26 each.  2Mbytes memory, and 640x480 resolution.  You'd never want to make a print from the files but that's not what I wanted it for.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car-2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Daleford||12-24-2001||09:35 PM|||| mbramble,  pics look good enough for me.<BR> How many megapixels is that camera?<BR>  -----Merry Christmas-----<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mbramble||12-24-2001||10:05 PM||||Not even one megapixel.  307K pixels.  But, good enuff for the Internet....  Especially at $26 !!<P>Available at <A HREF="http://www.computergeeks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.computergeeks.com</A>  and click on the Digital Camera link on the menu to the left.  (they are not shipping anything until 2 Jan)  Between three offices at work, we ordered 18 of these things after I got my first one in last week and we all got a chance to check it out.  You can also find them on ebay from $9 to $75 -- all the same camera.  Just go to ebay, and search for Largan....<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
